#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115075 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "51a437bf-2a11-5eba-a046-4770d41214ca" :question/math-academy-id "e-4720" :question/problem "Let ![](images/a9/a9f425a48a3ed8fabfce0eb1785ebdddc62d7dd3208ac302fd66a89b03e58cdb.svg) Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the identity matrix and replacing the second row with the result of adding $5$ times the first row to the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=5{R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation $R_2:=5R_1+ R_2$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115076 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/id #uuid "9927d1a6-a119-5987-9f49-5171a3f2e2d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-4721" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/11/11c345fde8fecb2e2a5459a0868ad8892e9067820de72f91601c1033858ca019.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115077 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "0f08f8aa-63e3-500a-987e-e9888b9b0479" :question/math-academy-id "e-4722" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2, \\qquad  R_2:=R_2+3R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is $R_2:=R_2+3R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/ea/ead4157a19d725334c44a55903b52bd12d7627e73696c2100efee52340347468.svg)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/ba/ba70270430d6c5606e816c16c606c8f3940742a48c95b0ad8a33f6c935da8cf6.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef7082b-a8cb-5f1a-919c-08c1470cb74b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+(-5){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263284} {:answer/id #uuid "26826c57-252e-56f3-928a-7ed1b119d8ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263335} {:answer/id #uuid "81bc10fa-ce64-5073-9d1d-50f07fae01cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-5{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264117} {:answer/id #uuid "aac4da94-090c-5cac-8faf-9b696938bf0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264461} {:answer/id #uuid "f36fc7b0-5e82-5868-91c8-65280ba1adb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f36fc7b0-5e82-5868-91c8-65280ba1adb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265138} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee672deb-35f0-517e-ab60-3ec6be1e3a3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29282155-f922-5de3-8efa-da8c96056d84" :question/math-academy-id "q-130838" :question/problem "Let $E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of the identity matrix and adding $-5$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029edf87-92f0-5f4d-857c-fbcd96d1ad44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263022} {:answer/id #uuid "04c58135-ba05-51f9-b009-72ffcc1bed2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263044} {:answer/id #uuid "92720e0d-2494-5493-a17f-d03095b968db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 18\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264255} {:answer/id #uuid "a462712d-421d-50ca-982e-193a070b7aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264401} {:answer/id #uuid "e44c943e-a381-50e6-92bb-55c088607ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04c58135-ba05-51f9-b009-72ffcc1bed2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263044} :answer-field/id #uuid "d138b62f-6f1b-544f-a0dd-55662c209a48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a1edd9d-9d16-504c-8084-c1f6f0fde2fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-130853" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=18{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=18{R}_{1}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=18{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115741 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-fi